Strawberries left after the smoothie:
$$ 3\tfrac{1}{2} - \tfrac{1}{4} = \tfrac{14}{4} - \tfrac{1}{4} = \tfrac{13}{4} = 3\tfrac{1}{4}
Half of the remaining strawberries go to the pancakes:
$$ \tfrac{1}{2} \times \tfrac{13}{4} = \tfrac{13}{8} = 1\tfrac{5}{8}
ANSWER: 1 5/8 cups

Total length of ribbon:
$$ 5.75 + 11.75 = 17.5 \text{ ft}
Cost per foot = total cost ÷ total length:
$$ \dfrac{\text{P}10.50}{17.5} = \text{P}0.60 \text{ per foot}
ANSWER: P0.60 per foot

Distance per liter = distance ÷ liters:
$$ \dfrac{48.3 \text{ km}}{2.3 \text{ L}} = 21 \text{ km/L}
ANSWER: 21 kilometers

Length of each part = total length ÷ number of parts:
$$ 35.14 \div 7 = 5.02 \text{ m}
ANSWER: 5.02 meters

Below the surface is negative. Starting at -9 ft and diving 8 ft more:
$$ -9 - 8 = -17 \text{ ft}
ANSWER: -17 feet

Drive to the museum:
$$ 11{:}15 + 0{:}30 = 11{:}45 \text{ A.M.}
Stay at the museum:
$$ 11{:}45 + 3{:}45 = 15{:}30 = 3{:}30 \text{ P.M.}
ANSWER: 3:30 pm

Total playing time:
$$ 2\text{ h} + 45\text{ min} + 2\text{ h }15\text{ min} = 5\text{ h}
Work backward from the finishing time:
$$ 7{:}00 \text{ P.M.} - 5\text{ h} = 2{:}00 \text{ P.M.}
ANSWER: 2:00 pm

Three digits after the decimal point means thousandths.
$$ 587.765 = \text{587 and 765 thousandths}
ANSWER: Five hundred eighty-seven and seven hundred sixty-five thousandths.

Divide 3/6 of a pack equally among 5 nieces:
$$ \tfrac{3}{6} \div 5 = \tfrac{3}{6} \times \tfrac{1}{5} = \tfrac{3}{30} = \tfrac{1}{10}
ANSWER: 1/10

Stacy and 6 friends = 7 people.
$$ \tfrac{3}{4} \div 7 = \tfrac{3}{4} \times \tfrac{1}{7} = \tfrac{3}{28} \text{ kg}
ANSWER: 3/28

1 week = 7 days:
$$ 92 \times 7 = 644 \text{ days}
ANSWER: 644 days

Average = total weight ÷ total number of chickens.
$$ \text{Hens: } 26 \times 40 = 1{,}040 \text{ kg}
$$ \text{Roosters: } 14 \times 35 = 490 \text{ kg}
$$ \dfrac{1{,}040 + 490}{26 + 14} = \dfrac{1{,}530}{40} = 38.25 \text{ kg}
ANSWER: 38.25 kg

Divide the dough among 24 pieces:
$$ \tfrac{3}{2} \div 24 = \tfrac{3}{2} \times \tfrac{1}{24} = \tfrac{3}{48} = \tfrac{1}{16} \text{ kg}
ANSWER: 1/16 kg

Three digits after the decimal point means thousandths.
$$ 376.504 = \text{376 and 504 thousandths}
ANSWER: three hundred seventy-six and five hundred four thousandths

Even numbers greater than 2 on a die: 4 and 6.
$$ P = \dfrac{2}{6} = \dfrac{1}{3}
